=== Democratic Party ===
A total of eight people from the Democratic Party announced their bid for the presidential race as of 28 April. Presidential hopefuls included former prime minister [[Norovyn Altankhuyag]], [[Rinchinnyamyn Amarjargal]], former [[Chairman of the Democratic Party (Mongolia)|party chairman]] [[Dambiin Dorligjav]], former [[Mayor of Ulaanbaatar|Ulaanbaatar mayor]] [[Erdeniin Bat-Üül]], historian [[Bat-Erdeniin Batbayar]] (colloquially known as Baabar),<ref>{{Cite web |last=Г |first=Батмандах |date=2017-04-12 |title=Б.Баабар Ерөнхийлөгчид нэр дэвшихээ зарлав |url=https://news.mn/r/762557/ |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=News.MN |language=mn}}</ref> and [[Khaltmaagiin Battulga]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Г |first=Батмандах |date=2017-04-28 |title=Mongolian DP nominees for presidential election |url=https://news.mn/en/763983/ |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=News.MN |language=en}}</ref> Out of the eight nominees, six people registered to compete in the primaries on 2 May.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Т |first=Өлзийбаяр |date=2017-05-02 |title=ТАНИЛЦ: Ерөнхийлөгчийн сонгуульд АН-аас нэр дэвшигчид |url=https://ikon.mn/n/100o |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=ikon.mn |language=mn}}</ref>

The DP chose Battulga as its nominee for the 2017 presidential election during its VIII Convention, which took place from 2nd to 4th of May.<ref name=":2" /> The DP candidate was picked via a poll held during the convention; Battulga, who had the highest score, was chosen.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Г |first=Даша |date=2017-05-04 |title=АН: Х.Баттулга дотоод сунгаанд тэргүүлжээ |url=https://eagle.mn/r/28639 |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=eagle.mn |language=mn}}</ref>
