| image2            = 2017 presidential election campaign poster of DP candidate Kh.Battulga.jpg
| image3            = 2017 presidential election campaign poster of MPRP candidate S.Ganbaatar.jpg
| image4            = 
| footer            = Campaign posters of [[Miyeegombyn Enkhbold]] (top left), [[Khaltmaagiin Battulga]] (top right), and [[Sainkhuugiin Ganbaatar]] (bottom) in [[Ulaanbaatar]]
}}
Candidates for the election had 18 days, 24 hours before the election was conducted on 26 June, to campaign after being registered by the GEC. Campaigning officially started on 27 May when all three candidates received their candidate ID cards from the GEC.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Э |first=Энхмаа |date=2017-02-18 |title=ДОЛОО ХОНОГИЙН ТОЙМ: Ерөнхийлөгчийн сонгуулийн сурталчилгаа эхэллээ |url=https://gogo.mn/r/xg27o |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=gogo.mn |language=mn}}</ref>

Battulga, a [[Judo|judoka]] and businessman, campaigned on a "Mongolia First" policy.<ref name=":6">{{Cite web |date=2017-06-26 |title=Mongolia's Ruling Party Candidate Loses in Presidential Race |url=https://www.voanews.com/a/mongolias-ruling-party-candidate-loses-in-presidential-race-/3917155.html |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=Voice of America |publisher=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> Political analysts drew similarities between Battulga's populist campaign and [[U.S. President]] [[Donald Trump]]'s [[Donald Trump 2016 presidential campaign|2016 campaign]].<ref name=":7">{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Marissa |date=2017-07-31 |title=Beyond “Populism without Party Platforms”: Mongolians’ Politics Beyond Ulaanbaatar |url=https://blogs.ubc.ca/mongolia/2017/politics-beyond-ulaanbaatar/ |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=Mongolia Focus |language=en-US}}</ref>

Ganbaatar, meanwhile, campaigned on [[resource nationalism]].<ref name=":6" /> Prior to and during his presidential candidacy, he strongly positioned himself against the current [[The Establishment|establishment]] politics and alleged MPP-DP [[cabal]].<ref name=":7" /> 

On 23 May, a video of Ganbaatar receiving a 50 million [[South Korean won|KRW]] (equivalent to 100 million MNT) donation from a South Korean citizen was uploaded anonymously and spread across social media.<ref name=":10">{{Cite web |date=2017-06-23 |title=Ерөнхийлөгчийн сонгуулийн адал явдал |url=https://www.unuudur.mn/a/97766 |access-date=2026-03-07 |website=www.unuudur.mn |language=mn}}</ref> According to the Law on Election, a candidate is prohibited from receiving donations from a foreign country, company, or citizen. The [[National Police Agency (Mongolia)|National Police Agency]] confirmed the recording as real and transferred the case to the court of Bayanzurkh District the following day, on 22 June.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kh |first=Kugershin |date=2017-06-23 |title=Case of presidential canditate S.Ganbaatar to be re-investigated |url=http://mongolia.gogo.mn/r/434kv |access-date=2026-03-06 |website=gogo.mn |language=en}}</ref> The court, without enough time, allowed Ganbaatar to remain on the ballot and later finalized the case after the election<ref>{{Cite web |last=R |first=Adiyasuren |date=2017-06-26 |title=Case of S.Ganbaatar will be finalized after the election |url=http://mongolia.gogo.mn/r/gx0yd |access-date=2026-03-06 |website=gogo.mn |language=en}}</ref> in October 2017.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ш |first=Чимэг |date=2017-10-16 |title=УИХ-ын гишүүн асан С.Ганбаатарыг шүүж байна |url=https://news.mn/r/512222/ |access-date=2026-03-07 |website=News.MN |language=mn}}</ref>

=== Debates ===
[[File:2017 Mongolian presidential debate.png|thumb|Left to right: [[Sainkhüügiin Ganbaatar|Sainkhuugiin Ganbaatar]] ([[Mongolian People's Revolutionary Party (2010)|MPRP]]), [[Miyeegombyn Enkhbold]] ([[Mongolian People's Party|MPP]]), [[Khaltmaagiin Battulga]] ([[Democratic Party (Mongolia)|DP]]) during the 2017 presidential debate|294x294px]]
The three candidates agreed to participate in a two-hour-long debate on the last day of campaigning.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mendee |date=2017-06-25 |title=Presidential Debate or FAQ? |url=https://mongoliafocus.com/2017/06/presidential-debate-issues/ |access-date=2026-02-16 |website=Mongolia Focus |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-06-24 |title=LIVE: Ерөнхийлөгчийн сонгуулийн мэтгэлцээн-2017 |url=https://itoim.mn/article/live-%D0%B5%D1%80%D3%A9%D0%BD%D1%85%D0%B8%D0%B9%D0%BB%D3%A9%D0%B3%D1%87%D0%B8%D0%B9%D0%BD-%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B9%D0%BD-%D0%BC%D1%8D%D1%82%D0%B3%D1%8D%D0%BB%D1%86%D1%8D%D1%8D%D0%BD/9473 |access-date=2026-02-16 |website=itoim.mn |language=mn}}</ref> The presidential debate was conducted and broadcast by the [[Mongolian National Broadcaster]] (MNB) on 24 June at 21:00 PM, four days before the election. Prior to the 2017 presidential debate, the MNB received the debate questions from the public via an online portal from 22 June 9:00 AM to 23 June 24:00 AM.<ref>{{Cite news |last= |first= |date=2017-06-22 |title=Монгол Улсын Ерөнхийлөгчийн сонгууль-2017 халз мэтгэлцээний асуултыг хүлээн авч байна |url=http://www.mnb.mn:80/i/117755 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180706001906/http://www.mnb.mn:80/i/117755 |archive-date=2018-07-06 |access-date=2026-02-16 |work=[[Mongolian National Broadcaster]] |language=mn}}</ref>

Battulga and Enkhbold advanced to the second round, with Battulga overperforming both Enkhbold and Ganbaatar by around 8 per cent. On June 28, the GEC announced that the second round will be held on the 7th of July, before the traditional [[Naadam]] festival.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-06-28 |title=Сонгуулийн дахин санал хураалтыг долдугаар сарын 7-ны өдөр болголоо |url=https://www.unuudur.mn/a/97878 |access-date=2026-03-06 |website=www.unuudur.mn |language=mn}}</ref>

