== Aftermath ==
On 8 July, before the official final results came out, MPP candidate Enkhbold, MPP secretary general [[Dashzegviin Amarbayasgalan]], and MPP caucus chairman [[Damdiny Khayankhyarvaa]] conceded victory to Battulga during a press conference.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Soni |first=Sharad |date=2017-08-11 |title=Mongolia’s new president is Mongolia first and China last |url=https://eastasiaforum.org/2017/08/11/mongolias-new-president-is-mongolia-first-and-china-last/ |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=[[East Asia Forum]] |language=en}}</ref> Enkhbold, as chairman of the State Great Khural, noted that when the GEC presents the final results to parliament, he will convene an [[Special session|extraordinary session]] to quickly organize the presidential inauguration ceremony. He also thanked his voters, supporters, and party workers at the end of the press conference.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ж |first=Тэгшжаргал |date=2017-07-08 |title=М.Энхболд: Сонгуулийн дүнг ХҮНДЭТГЭН хүлээж авч байна |url=https://ub.life/p/8799 |access-date=2026-02-18 |website=UB Life |language=mn}}</ref>

The inauguration ceremony of Khaltmaagiin Battulga as the fifth president of Mongolia was held at the [[Government Palace (Mongolia)|Government Palace]] on 10 July 2017. During the ceremony, the extraordinary session of the State Great Khural, chaired by Enkhbold, also took place. Battulga took the [[Oath of office|presidential oath of office]] in front of the State Great Khural and received the [[State seal of Mongolia]] from the outgoing fourth president, [[Tsakhiagiin Elbegdorj]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-07-10 |title=Шинээр сонгогдсон Ерөнхийлөгч тангараг өргөж, Улсын Их Хурлын ээлжит бус чуулган өндөрлөлөө |url=https://www.parliament.mn/nn/17876/ |access-date=2026-03-07 |website=State Great Hural /Parliament/ of Mongolia |language=mn}}</ref>

